Chapter: SpikeTruckMain
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Poc chapter Spike
  cites Poc chapter SpikePrint

 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. The two truck stills, and the entry that first made the
 split: `SpikeMain`'s header holds the rule and the measurements.

 THE ORIGINAL EVIDENCE WAS THE NATIVE CEILING. Six viewpoints in one process came
 to within a rounding error of the 4 GiB reserve, and adding a seventh exhausted
 it:

     cx heap: exhausted at 4294965457 + 7000 of 4294967296

 IT WAS READ AS A PAGE-PERFECT ILLUSTRATION OF C6 AND IT WAS HALF THAT. The bump
 heap does never reclaim, so the peak really was the total -- but the total was
 quadratic, because every printer concatenated left to right and so allocated the
 sum of its own suffixes. C17 has the measurement: the same two frames peaked at
 3.5 GB before the halving fix and 133 MB after it, byte for byte the same output.
 An allocator that never frees is very good at hiding an algorithmic mistake
 behind itself.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (scene-line "truck-day" u-truck-day)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-near u-truck-day spike-truck-lead) 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "truck-dusk" u-truck-dusk)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-near u-truck-dusk spike-truck-lead) 0)
  end
